                             <p><p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Applications are invited for admission to the Ph.D. Programme for the July 2026 Session. The list of disciplines, discipline-wise number of seats (category-wise) available, and eligibility criteria are provided in the Information Brochure.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>The Ph.D. Programme is offered in compliance with the UGC (Minimum Standards and Procedure for Award of Ph.D. Degree) Regulations, 2022, and amendments thereto issued from time to time.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>IGNOU offers the Ph.D. Programme under two categories: Full-Time and Part-Time. Candidates admitted under both categories shall be required to attend the Course Work classes as per the IGNOU Ph.D. Guidelines at the respective Schools of Studies located at the IGNOU Headquarters, Maidan Garhi, New Delhi. The Course Work shall be conducted during the first six months of admission and will be held only at the IGNOU Campus, New Delhi. Students are required to attend the Course Work classes on a regular basis. A minimum of 80% attendance in the Course Work is mandatory.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>The minimum and maximum duration of the Ph.D. Programme shall be three years and six years, respectively. However, women candidates and Persons with Disabilities (PwD) having 40% or more disability (or &ldquo;severe&rdquo; where the percentage is not defined) shall be allowed an additional period of two years beyond the maximum duration for completion of the Programme.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>At present, IGNOU does not provide hostel facilities for Ph.D. students. Candidates shall be required to make their own arrangements for accommodation and stay in Delhi during the Course Work and other academic requirements.&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Candidates who are employed and wish to pursue the Part-Time Ph.D. Programme must obtain a No Objection Certificate (NOC) from their employer in the prescribed format available in the Information Brochure. Submission of the NOC is mandatory at the time of interview (wherever applicable).&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Instructions for Candidates &ndash; Ph.D. Admission July 2026</span></strong></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Before filling the Online Application Form, candidates are advised to carefully read the Information Brochure and ensure that they fulfil the prescribed eligibility criteria for the discipline applied for.</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Step 1: New User Registration</span></strong></p>
<ol style="margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm;" start="1" type="1">
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Register yourself on the admission portal using a <strong>valid and active Email ID</strong> and <strong>Mobile Number</strong>.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>All future communications, including login credentials, application status, examination/interview updates, and admission-related information, will be sent to the registered Email ID and Mobile Number.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Candidates are advised to keep the registered Email ID and Mobile Number active throughout the admission process.</span></li>
</ol>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Step 2: Keep Documents Ready Before Applying</span></strong></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Candidates should keep the following scanned documents ready before starting the application process:</span></p>
<ul style="margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm;" type="disc">
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Recent Passport Size Colour Photograph</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Signature of the Candidate</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Aadhaar Card / Valid Photo Identity Proof</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Date of Birth Certificate / Class X Certificate</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Marksheets and Certificates of Qualifying Examinations</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Category Certificate (SC/ST/OBC-NCL/EWS), if applicable</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>PwBD Certificate, if applicable</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>UGC-NET/JRF Certificate, wherever applicable</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Experience Certificate/NOC from Employer (for Part-Time candidates), wherever applicable</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Any other supporting document required for eligibility verification</span></li>
</ul>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Important Instructions</span></strong></p>
<ol style="margin-bottom:0cm;margin-top:0cm;" start="1" type="1">
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Ensure that all uploaded documents are clear, legible, and self-attested wherever required.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Enter all details carefully as submitted information cannot be modified after final submission.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Verify eligibility, category details, and programme selection before making payment.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Keep a scanned copy of all documents and payment details readily available while filling the form.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>After successful submission, download and save the completed Application Form and Payment Receipt for future reference.</span></li>
    <li style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Submission of the application does not automatically confer eligibility or admission. Applications shall be scrutinized as per the University rules and regulations.</span></li>
</ol>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>Note:</span></strong><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>&nbsp;Candidates are advised to use the latest version of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, or any other browser for a smooth application submission experience.</span></p>
<p style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:0cm;margin-bottom:8.0pt;margin-left:0cm;line-height:115%;font-size:16px;font-family:"Aptos",sans-serif;text-align:justify;'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif;'>&nbsp;</span></p>
